WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.539 --> 00:00:04.810
So on Tuesday, Donald Trump did this video
screed where he had sort of like conflicting

00:00:04.810 --> 00:00:11.230
and confused reasons for which he was threatening
to veto the second coronavirus stimulus package

00:00:11.230 --> 00:00:12.240
on Wednesday.

00:00:12.240 --> 00:00:14.670
He did veto that package.

00:00:14.670 --> 00:00:20.210
And one of the things Donald Trump said he
wanted is a 2000 dollar stimulus check rather

00:00:20.210 --> 00:00:22.700
than a 600 dollar stimulus check.

00:00:22.700 --> 00:00:28.099
Now, very conveniently, many Democrats, including
our friend Roxana.

00:00:28.099 --> 00:00:33.020
Have been talking about thousand dollars per
person for a while, and as soon as Donald

00:00:33.020 --> 00:00:37.070
Trump said, I want to grand, many Democrats
said great, let's work together on it, we're

00:00:37.070 --> 00:00:38.410
ready to do it.

00:00:38.410 --> 00:00:41.490
But the Republican Party has blocked an attempt.

00:00:41.490 --> 00:00:47.130
Democrats did move to increase the size of
the checks when Trump said, let's do two thousand

00:00:47.130 --> 00:00:54.340
and it is not going to happen because yesterday
House Republicans blocked the attempt by Democrats

00:00:54.340 --> 00:00:57.550
to do two thousand dollar payments.

00:00:57.550 --> 00:01:04.350
And now we are simply waiting on whether the
House will vote to override Trump's veto on

00:01:04.350 --> 00:01:13.220
Monday and whether, if that happens, the Senate
will vote to override Trump's veto on Tuesday.

00:01:13.220 --> 00:01:16.940
But it is it's just not going anywhere.

00:01:16.940 --> 00:01:22.350
The Republican Party has been arguing for
less and less money.

00:01:22.350 --> 00:01:28.530
And the House tried to pass two thousand dollar
payments on Christmas Eve day.

00:01:28.530 --> 00:01:36.050
So yesterday during the day, they had a brief
meeting of the House where Democrats tried

00:01:36.050 --> 00:01:40.960
to approve two thousand dollar payments by
unanimous consent, which means any one lawmaker

00:01:40.960 --> 00:01:41.960
can block it.

00:01:41.960 --> 00:01:45.970
It's not a 50 plus or supermajority or whatever.

00:01:45.970 --> 00:01:50.659
It is simply any one Republican, any one lawmaker
can block it.

00:01:50.659 --> 00:01:55.659
Congressman Steny Hoyer, Democrat, offered
the proposal from the floor and it was blocked

00:01:55.659 --> 00:01:59.770
by House Minority Leader Kevin McCarthy.

00:01:59.770 --> 00:02:01.220
And that is it.

00:02:01.220 --> 00:02:08.739
So we there's really no expectation at this
point that that is going to happen under Trump's

00:02:08.739 --> 00:02:09.739
watch.

00:02:09.739 --> 00:02:15.829
House Speaker Nancy Pelosi said that on Monday
she will do a recorded vote on the two thousand

00:02:15.829 --> 00:02:16.829
dollar payments.

00:02:16.829 --> 00:02:21.569
But I mean, it's not going to make any difference
at this point in time.

00:02:21.569 --> 00:02:29.489
Democrats continue to tell Trump, just sign
the bill and let's I mean, listen, one of

00:02:29.489 --> 00:02:36.249
the other problems here is why is the government
funding bill part of the same vote as the

00:02:36.249 --> 00:02:38.049
covid stimulus bill?

00:02:38.049 --> 00:02:41.659
We know why this is a common thing that's
done in Congress.

00:02:41.659 --> 00:02:46.379
The idea is, if you're against a bunch of
stuff one party wants to do, you say let's

00:02:46.379 --> 00:02:49.590
join this vote with the stuff we want to do.

00:02:49.590 --> 00:02:51.920
You do one, vote for both bills.

00:02:51.920 --> 00:02:55.849
And then 20 years later, much like we've seen
happen with Bernie and Joe Biden and others,

00:02:55.849 --> 00:03:01.409
when you're asked why did you vote in favor
of Bill A. and you say, listen, I wasn't really

00:03:01.409 --> 00:03:07.310
in favor of Bill, I was in favor of Bill B,
but our colleagues on the other side said

00:03:07.310 --> 00:03:10.650
the only way they would support it is if we
wrapped it up with Bill.

00:03:10.650 --> 00:03:15.279
I found it so important to get the people
six hundred dollars instead of zero that I

00:03:15.279 --> 00:03:16.279
conceded.

00:03:16.279 --> 00:03:20.049
I said, I'll give them Billey because they're
giving me Bill B, which I think is the right

00:03:20.049 --> 00:03:21.889
bill for for helping people.

00:03:21.889 --> 00:03:22.889
This is politics.

00:03:22.889 --> 00:03:23.939
This is how it always works.

00:03:23.939 --> 00:03:24.939
It's disgusting.

00:03:24.939 --> 00:03:30.349
There's no actual reason that you couldn't
have one vote on covid stimulus and then separately

00:03:30.349 --> 00:03:32.079
one vote on government funding.

00:03:32.079 --> 00:03:34.680
But that is the way that they have done it.

00:03:34.680 --> 00:03:39.430
And one of the interesting sort of little
details is we talked yesterday about how Donald

00:03:39.430 --> 00:03:47.010
Trump has turned on basically everybody around
him, Mike Pence, Mike Pompeo, he's he believes

00:03:47.010 --> 00:03:51.349
none of them are supporting him in his bid
to overturn the election results.

00:03:51.349 --> 00:03:53.760
Mitch McConnell is also on that list.

00:03:53.760 --> 00:03:57.299
And Mitch McConnell has been against more
stimulus for months.

00:03:57.299 --> 00:04:02.290
And when it's a conversation about stimulus,
he wants the smallest possible stimulus since

00:04:02.290 --> 00:04:05.969
Trump suggested the two thousand dollar payments.

00:04:05.969 --> 00:04:14.769
Mitch McConnell has been silent about the
demand for the two thousand dollar payments.

00:04:14.769 --> 00:04:18.450
And it is just, you know, who really loses
here?

00:04:18.450 --> 00:04:19.450
It's the people.

00:04:19.450 --> 00:04:20.450
Right.

00:04:20.450 --> 00:04:28.240
And this is why when we talk about political
posturing by either side, when we talk about

00:04:28.240 --> 00:04:34.730
all of these different public moves that do
nothing to actually get help to people to

00:04:34.730 --> 00:04:44.320
be any closer to a reality, we have to remember
that a bunch of this stuff is almost almost

00:04:44.320 --> 00:04:48.650
as bad on the Democratic side as the Republican
side.

00:04:48.650 --> 00:04:53.300
So we'll see what happens Monday with the
House vote on overriding Trump's veto.

00:04:53.300 --> 00:04:57.600
We'll see what happens Tuesday conditionally
with the Senate voting to override that same

00:04:57.600 --> 00:04:58.860
veto.

00:04:58.860 --> 00:05:03.990
And maybe by mid-January, payments could be
going to people.

00:05:03.990 --> 00:05:07.020
It will take a couple, at least a couple of
weeks.

00:05:07.020 --> 00:05:12.330
It is believed once if and when this is approved
for money to get into anybody's hands.

00:05:12.330 --> 00:05:16.610
So certainly twenty, twenty one not this is
not going to be twenty, twenty money in the

00:05:16.610 --> 00:05:19.070
best case at all.

